 "brief": {
  "short_answer": "FAA guidance requires attempting to reestablish control link and, if unsuccessful, initiating emergency or contingency procedures for loss of control link. Manufacturer manuals for the involved models describe signal-loss behaviors such as RTH, hover, or land, with conditions based on lighting, vision systems, or battery state. Incident reports show real-world cases where lost links triggered RTH or other failsafes, sometimes with interference factors. Gaps exist between generic regulatory guidance and model-specific behaviors, and between verified manuals and unverified incident reports.",
  "sections": [
   {
    "section": "faa",
    "label": "FAA guidance",
    "status": "drafted",
    "abstain_reason": null,
    "claims": [
     {
      "text": "When a control link is lost, operators should try to reestablish the control link, and if it cannot be reestablished, start emergency or contingency procedures for loss of control link.",
      "citations": [
       "faa_ac_107_2a_2022_c0228",
       "faa_ac_107_2a_2022_c0227"
      ],
      "quote": "Example: Try to reestablish control link connection with the small unmanned aircraft. If connection cannot be reestablished, start emergency or contingency procedures for loss of control link.",
      "conditions": [
       "None specified"
      ],
      "assessment": "supported",
      "claim_id": "C001",
      "section": "faa",
      "tier": "official",
      "incident_label": null
     },
     {
      "text": "Remote controller link loss may require pre-determined procedures depending on whether VLOS can be regained; loss of VLOS guidance requires following pre-determined procedures.",
      "citations": [
       "faa_ac_107_2a_2022_c0049"
      ],
      "quote": "If the remote PIC cannot regain VLOS, the remote PIC or person manipulating the controls should follow pre-determined procedures for the loss of VLOS.",
      "conditions": [],
      "assessment": "supported",
      "claim_id": "C002",
      "section": "faa",
      "tier": "official",
      "incident_label": null
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "section": "manual:DJI Matrice 30T",
    "label": "DJI Matrice 30T manual",
    "status": "drafted",
    "abstain_reason": null,
    "claims": [
     {
      "text": "In DJI Matrice 30T, the action when the remote controller signal is lost can be set to RTH, land, or hover; RTH remains active even if the link is restored, unless canceled by user actions.",
      "citations": [
       "manual:DJI Matrice 30T"
      ],
      "quote": "The action of the aircraft when the remote controller signal is lost can be set to RTH, land, or hover in Camera View > > > Signal Lost Action in DJI Pilot 2 . The aircraft will remain in RTH even if the remote controller signal is restored.",
      "conditions": [
       "Settings determine Signal Lost Action"
      ],
      "assessment": "supported",
      "claim_id": "C003",
      "section": "manual:DJI Matrice 30T",
      "tier": "manufacturer",
      "incident_label": null
     },
     {
      "text": "In DJI Matrice 30T, if RTH is canceled, the Intelligent Battery may not have enough power, risking a crash or loss; auto-landing may occur if power insufficient.",
      "citations": [
       "manual:DJI Matrice 30T"
      ],
      "quote": "If RTH is canceled following the warning, the Intelligent Battery may not have enough power for the aircraft to land safely, which may lead to the aircraft crashing or being lost.",
      "conditions": [],
      "assessment": "supported",
      "claim_id": "C004",
      "section": "manual:DJI Matrice 30T",
      "tier": "manufacturer",
      "incident_label": null
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "section": "manual:DJI Matrice 4T",
    "label": "DJI Matrice 4T manual",
    "status": "drafted",
    "abstain_reason": null,
    "claims": [
     {
      "text": "DJI Matrice 4T guidance describes Failsafe RTH when signal is lost, with RTH path displayed if lighting allows vision system; otherwise hover and Original Route RTH.",
      "citations": [
       "manual:DJI Matrice 4T"
      ],
      "quote": "Loss of remote controller signal When the remote controller signal is lost, the aircraft will automatically initiate Failsafe RTH if the Signal Lost Action is set to RTH. When the lighting and environment conditions are suitable for the vision system, DJI Pilot 2 will display the RTH path... The aircraft will remain in RTH even if the remote controller signal is restored. DJI Pilot 2 will update the RTH path accordingly. When the lighting and environment conditions are unsuitable for the vision system, the aircraft will brake and hover, then enter Original Route RTH.",
      "conditions": [
       "Lighting/vision conditions affect RTH path"
      ],
      "assessment": "supported",
      "claim_id": "C005",
      "section": "manual:DJI Matrice 4T",
      "tier": "manufacturer",
      "incident_label": null
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "section": "manual:Autel EVO Max 4N",
    "label": "Autel EVO Max 4N manual",
    "status": "drafted",
    "abstain_reason": null,
    "claims": [
     {
      "text": "Autel EVO Max 4N describes Signal Lost behavior including Return to Home, Hover, and Land, with reconnection attempts and a preset Signal Loss Action.",
      "citations": [
       "manual:Autel EVO Max 4N"
      ],
      "quote": "The drone\u2019s Signal Lost behavior options include Return to Home, Hover, and Land. Signal Loss Action options include Continue mission and Auto RTH.",
